SPlus. I have this program installed and running on a DecSystem 5500
RISC Computer System. This program uses up the resources of any computer
it is run on. It doesn't clean up swap memory during loops and it tends
to use up all the system memory unless you limit the system memory
somehow. I have adjusted the swap size, data size, and other kernel
parameters to make this program behave in a reasonable manner. Using
csh's limit commands seem to help but I would like feedback from other
