> Any expansion slots?

	Depending on your choice of graphics subsystem, two to zero
	TURBOchannel slots are available.  Don't be surprised if we
	solve the zero availables with the PXG Turbo problem someday.

	The memory is expandable up to 420 MB using the 32 MB 
	MS02-CA memory module.  Using the MS02-AA 8 MB memory
	module it's 120 MB.  The two can't (CAN NOT) be mixed.

	Currently available TURBOchannel options are a thick-
	wire Ethernet adapter and a SCSI controller.  I think
	an FDDI adapter is also available, but it isn't listed
	in the catalog I've got.  The catalog does mention a
	VME I/O expansion box, but there doesn't seem to be
	corresponding TURBOchannel device (yet).

	Supported SCSI devices available include:

		RZ55 - 332 MB disk.
		RZ56 - 665 MB disk.
		RZ57 - 1.0 GB disk.
		TLZ04 - 1.2 GB 4 mm digital audio tape (RDAT).
		TKZ08 - 2.2 GB 8 mm tape.
		RRD40 - 600 MB CDROM.
		RX23 - 1.44 MB diskette drive.
		RX33 - 1.2 MB diskette drive.
		TZ30 - 95 MB cartridge tape (TK50).

	The RZ disks, RX diskettes and TZ30 come in a dual drive
