In article <1991Mar25.004654.24984@wpi.WPI.EDU>, paranoid@wpi.WPI.EDU (Paranoid) writes:
> 
> 	After running SYSGEN, I ran usat like manual says, and many of
> 	the programs fail with:
> 
> 	Illegal instruction - core dumped
> 
> 	Programs like awk, iostat, and a few others seem to fail.

  Two possibilities:

  1) You're missing some hardware feature. For example, I know that 2BSD
     insists on having a floating point unit. The FPP is a M7093 in slot
     3.

  2) You've got some broken hardware. Try running the diagnostics for the
     11/44 (if you have a diagnostic tape/disk). The 44-specific diags are
     named K-something. So, try KKAA, KKAB, KKAC, KFPA, KFPB and also ZMSP
     to test memory.

